# ART context: <train name>

Lives at `.artstack/art.md` in the repository your team works in. Commit it so
the whole team reads one copy.

Refresh this file at each planning-interval boundary, and give that refresh a
named owner on the same checklist as the planning event itself. Everything here
is train-level truth that every skill reads. Keep it under two pages. No
secrets, no credentials, no customer data.

Stale context is worse than none: it is confidently wrong and nobody notices.

